sayoq fk6fouc fod5ikn faaz57k fl43uef fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Needs someone else</h4><ul class="kg-catalog-plain"></ul><span class="fui-Caption1 fui-Text ___13vod6f_1082073 fk6fouc fy9rknc fwrc4pm figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Endorsement (Promoted, Certified) stays a person&#x27;s decision: Krusgraph never sets or asks for it.</span><div class="kg-catalog-files"></div></section>"`;

exports[`WB11: the next steps' cards > match the snapshot 1`] = `
"<section class="kg-next" aria-labelledby="kg-next-title"><h2 id="kg-next-title" class="fui-Subtitle2 fui-Text ___i24qii0_1tsayoq fk6fouc fod5ikn faaz57k fl43uef fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Next, with other Fabric workloads</h2><span data-say="thinker" class="fui-Body1 fui-Text ___c56hd20_oafdhs0 fk6fouc fkhj508 f1i3iumi figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649"><strong>Thinker:</strong> Proven on the rows (checked 2026-11-17 00:40 UTC): 6 of 6 keys unique, 7 of 7 links holding, 232 rows counted in 6 tables, 0 orphans, 0 duplicate keys.</span><span data-say="onto" class="fui-Body1 fui-Text ___c56hd20_oafdhs0 fk6fouc fkhj508 f1i3iumi figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649"><strong>Onto:</strong> Summing an orders amount over order items would count each order about 2 times; sum order items per order first.</span><span class="fui-Caption1 fui-Text ___13vod6f_1082073 fk6fouc fy9rknc fwrc4pm figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Suggestions by rules from what was proven; no AI. A dry run comes before anything is created.</span><ul class="kg-next-list"><li class="kg-next-card" data-step="ds-features"><div class="kg-next-head"><span class="krusgraph-item-title kg-next-workload"><img class="krusgraph-item-icon" src="/assets/fabric-icons/notebook_24_item.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"/><img class="krusgraph-item-icon" src="/assets/fabric-icons/experiments_24_item.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"/><span class="fui-Caption1 fui-Text ___13vod6f_1082073 fk6fouc fy9rknc fwrc4pm figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Data Science · Notebook, Experiment</span></span><div class="fui-Badge r1iycov ___1jem4av_anf6qd0 f2vsrz6 ffmvakt fdmic9h f196y6m f1pev5xq fetptd8">Starter to download</div></div><h3 class="fui-Subtitle2 fui-Text ___i24qii0_1tsayoq fk6fouc fod5ikn faaz57k fl43uef fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Feature table at the grain of orders, with an Experiment</h3><span class="fui-Body1 fui-Text ___c56hd20_oafdhs0 fk6fouc fkhj508 f1i3iumi figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Your order_items → orders link is proven (134 rows, 0 orphans), so this notebook sums order_items per orders row first: one row per orders row, no total counted 2.2×.</span><span class="fui-Caption1 fui-Text ___13vod6f_1082073 fk6fouc fy9rknc fwrc4pm figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Dry run, then Create puts the notebook in this item&#x27;s workspace, attached to the data product&#x27;s lakehouse; or download it. Krusgraph trains no model.</span><div class="kg-next-actions"><span class="kg-file" data-file="orders_features.ipynb"><button type="button" aria-label="Download notebook (.ipynb): orders_features.ipynb" class="fui-Button r1f29ykk"><span class="fui-Button__icon rywnvv2 ___963sj20_1qpm2bl f1nizpg2"><svg fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-fui-icon="" class="fui-Icon ___9ctc0p0_1xvj9ao f1w7gpdv fez10in f1dd5bof" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M15.5 17a.5.5 0 0 1 .09 1H4.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.09-1H15.5M10 2a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.41V14.3l3.64-3.65a.5.5 0 0 1 .64-.06l.07.06c.17.17.2.44.06.63l-.06.07-4.5 4.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.25.14L10 16a.5.5 0 0 1-.4-.2l-4.46-4.45a.5.5 0 0 1 .64-.76l.07.06 3.65 3.64V2.5c0-.27.22-.5.5-.5" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>Download notebook (.ipynb)</button></span><button type="button" class="fui-Button r1f29ykk"><span class="fui-Button__icon rywnvv2 ___963sj20_1qpm2bl f1nizpg2"><svg fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-fui-icon="" class="fui-Icon ___9ctc0p0_1xvj9ao f1w7gpdv fez10in f1dd5bof" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M7 7H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h4a2 2 0 0 0 2-2h1a3 3 0 0 1-3 3H5a3 3 0 0 1-3-3V9a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h2zm8-5a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v6a3 3 0 0 1-3 3h-4a3 3 0 0 1-3-3V5a3 3 0 0 1 3-3zm-4 1a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h4a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>Copy the code</button></div><details class="kg-next-code"><summary><span class="fui-Caption1 fui-Text ___13vod6f_1082073 fk6fouc fy9rknc fwrc4pm figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Show the code</span></summary><pre># Krusgraph starter: a feature table at the grain of orders (one row per orders), for Data Science.
# Made by rules from the keys and links Krusgraph proved on shop_lh / shop (checked 2026-11-17T00:40Z):
#   orders: key order_id, unique in all 60 rows
#   order_items.order_id -&gt; orders: holds for all 134 rows, 0 orphans
#   134 order_items rows over 60 orders rows: a orders amount summed over order_items counts each orders 2.2x.
# Attach the notebook to the lakehouse shop_lh and run the cells in order. Nothing is written until cell 3.

# ----

from pyspark.sql import functions as F
from pyspark.sql.types import NumericType

parent = spark.read.table(&quot;\`shop\`.\`orders\`&quot;)
child = spark.read.table(&quot;\`shop\`.\`order_items\`&quot;)
key = &quot;order_id&quot;.split(&quot;,&quot;)

# 1. order_items summed per orders first: every numeric column of order_items except its keys and links (ids are not summed)
skip = set(&quot;order_id,line_no,product_id&quot;.split(&quot;,&quot;))
numeric = [f.name for f in child.schema.fields if isinstance(f.dataType, NumericType) and f.name not in skip]
per_parent = (child.groupBy(*&quot;order_id&quot;.split(&quot;,&quot;))
    .agg(F.count(F.lit(1)).alias(&quot;order_items_rows&quot;), *[F.sum(c).alias(f&quot;order_items_{c}_sum&quot;) for c in numeric])
    .withColumnsRenamed({&quot;order_id&quot;: &quot;order_id&quot;}))

# 2. joined once, on the proven key: one row per orders
features = parent.join(per_parent, on=key, how=&quot;left&quot;).fillna(0, subset=[&quot;order_items_rows&quot;])
display(features.limit(10))

# ----

# 3. the grain, checked before anything is written: one row per orders, so no total is doubled
n_parent, n_features = parent.count(), features.count()
assert n_features == n_parent, f&quot;{n_features} feature rows for {n_parent} orders rows: the grain is not one row per orders&quot;
assert features.select(*key).distinct().count() == n_features, &quot;the key repeats in the feature table&quot;
features.write.mode(&quot;overwrite&quot;).format(&quot;delta&quot;).saveAsTable(&quot;orders_features&quot;)
print(f&quot;orders_features: {n_features} rows, one per orders&quot;)

# ----

# 4. optional: an ML Experiment for the runs on this table. In a Fabric notebook, mlflow.set_experiment creates the
#    Experiment item in this workspace if it does not exist (Microsoft Learn, &quot;Machine learning experiment&quot;).
import mlflow
mlflow.set_experiment(&quot;orders_experiment&quot;)
with mlflow.start_run(run_name=&quot;feature table orders_features&quot;):
    mlflow.log_param(&quot;grain&quot;, &quot;orders&quot;)
    mlflow.log_param(&quot;source&quot;, &quot;shop_lh.shop&quot;)
    mlflow.log_metric(&quot;rows&quot;, n_features)
# Train your model on spark.read.table(&quot;orders_features&quot;) inside a run like this one; Krusgraph does not train or choose a model.</pre></details></li><li class="kg-next-card" data-step="pbi"><div class="kg-next-head"><span class="krusgraph-item-title kg-next-workload"><img class="krusgraph-item-icon" src="/assets/fabric-icons/semantic_model_24_item.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"/><img class="krusgraph-item-icon" src="/assets/fabric-icons/report_24_item.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"/><span class="fui-Caption1 fui-Text ___13vod6f_1082073 fk6fouc fy9rknc fwrc4pm figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Power BI · Semantic model, Report</span></span><div class="fui-Badge r1iycov ___172bkpj_b7iz950 f16xkysk faj9fo0 f161y7kd f1c8dzaj f1619yhw f1sl6hi9">Krusgraph builds it</div></div><h3 class="fui-Subtitle2 fui-Text ___i24qii0_1tsayoq fk6fouc fod5ikn faaz57k fl43uef fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Semantic model and report</h3><span class="fui-Body1 fui-Text ___c56hd20_oafdhs0 fk6fouc fkhj508 f1i3iumi figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">7 of 7 links hold with 0 orphans, so every relationship in the model is many-to-one onto a key proven unique.</span><div class="kg-next-actions"><button type="button" aria-label="Dry run: Semantic model and report" class="fui-Button r1f29ykk"><span class="fui-Button__icon rywnvv2 ___963sj20_1qpm2bl f1nizpg2"><svg fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-fui-icon="" class="fui-Icon ___9ctc0p0_1xvj9ao f1w7gpdv fez10in f1dd5bof" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M17.22 8.69a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 0 2.62l-10 5.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 5 15.5v-11A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 7.22 3.2zm-.48 1.75a.5.5 0 0 0 0-.88l-10-5.5A.5.5 0 0 0 6 4.5v11c0 .38.4.62.74.44z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>Dry run</button></div></li><li class="kg-next-card" data-step="agent"><div class="kg-next-head"><span class="krusgraph-item-title kg-next-workload"><img class="krusgraph-item-icon" src="/assets/fabric-icons/data_agent_24_item.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"/><span class="fui-Caption1 fui-Text ___13vod6f_1082073 fk6fouc fy9rknc fwrc4pm figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Data agent</span></span><div class="fui-Badge r1iycov ___172bkpj_b7iz950 f16xkysk faj9fo0 f161y7kd f1c8dzaj f1619yhw f1sl6hi9">Krusgraph builds it</div></div><h3 class="fui-Subtitle2 fui-Text ___i24qii0_1tsayoq fk6fouc fod5ikn faaz57k fl43uef fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">A data agent that answers in words</h3><span class="fui-Body1 fui-Text ___c56hd20_oafdhs0 fk6fouc fkhj508 f1i3iumi figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Its instructions are written from the 6 keys and 7 links you proved, with example questions to try before anyone relies on it.</span><span class="fui-Caption1 fui-Text ___13vod6f_1082073 fk6fouc fy9rknc fwrc4pm figsok6 fpgzoln f1w7gpdv f6juhto f1gl81tg f2jf649">Left unpublished, a draft only you see, unless you tick Publish.</span><div class="kg-next-actions"><button type="button" aria-label="Dry run: A data agent that answers in words" class="fui-Button r1f29ykk"><span class="fui-Button__icon rywnvv2 ___963sj20_1qpm2bl f1nizpg2"><svg fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-fui-icon="" class="fui-Icon ___9ctc0p0_1xvj9ao f1w7gpdv fez10in f1dd5bof" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M17.22 8.69a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 0 2.62l-10 5.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 5 15.5v-11A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 7.22 3.2zm-.48 1.75a.5.5 0 0 0 0-.88l-10-5.5A.5.5 0 0 0 6 4.5v11c0 .38.4.62.74.44z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>Dry run</button></div></li><li class="kg-next-card" data-step="factory"><div class="kg-next-head"><span class="krusgraph-item-title kg-next-workload"><img class="krusgraph-item-icon" src="/assets/fabric-icons/pipeline_24_item.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"/><img class="krusgraph-item-icon" src="/assets/fabric-icons/notebook_24_item.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20"/><span c